# Application PHPDoc

Follow `App\Services\Auth\Authentication` and `docs/phpdoc.md` for all new or edited PHP files in `app/`.

- Document every class and named method, including protected/private methods and constructors.
- Start with a meaningful English sentence describing behavior, not a repetition of the method name.
- Add one typed `@param` per parameter in signature order; separate the summary and parameter group with a blank PHPDoc line.
- Separate parameters from `@return` with a blank PHPDoc line. Include `@return void` for void methods and constructors.
- Place accurate `@throws` entries after `@return`; document escaping exceptions, not exceptions handled internally. Never copy exception tags blindly.
- Match nullable and union types; describe array keys/values using generics or shapes and use specific types when supported by the implementation.
- Preserve useful descriptions and framework annotations (`@method`, `@mixin`, `@use`, `@var`). Do not invent types or example credentials.
- Update PHPDoc in the same change as the implementation. Review summaries, parameter order, return types and exception behavior before finishing.
- Documentation-only changes must preserve executable PHP tokens. Do not alter signatures or behavior merely to match documentation.
